        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-devicelist" data-main="devices" data-sub="devicelist">
            <div class="info">
                One row per device, merged from the data already stored on this server - no command is sent to a
                device just to show this list. Click a column header to sort. The buttons in a row act on
                <strong>that one device</strong>; tick several devices and use the batch buttons to run one
                operation on all of them.
                <br><br>
                <strong>Restart</strong> and <strong>Reset</strong> are the only actions that reboot a machine. They are
                never batched and never automatic: a restart needs a grace period, a message to the logged-on user and
                the device name typed to confirm; a reset needs a fresh read-only check first. Everything else here
                (updates, OS updates, upgrades, Windows Update repair, license collection) never reboots - a needed
                restart is only reported.
            </div>
            <div class="info">
                One row per device, built from the data already stored on this server - opening this page sends no
                command to any device. Hover any button and its explanation appears in the box at the lower right.
                <br><br>
                <strong>Reboot</strong> and a <strong>reset</strong> are the only actions that restart a machine: never
                batched, never automatic, always per device and with the device name typed to confirm. Everything else
                here (software updates, OS updates, upgrades, Windows Update repair, license collection) never reboots -
                a needed restart is only reported. The fleet OS buttons, the upgrade reference and the OS update log are
                at the bottom of this page; <em>Details</em> opens everything stored about one device on demand and is
                kept in memory while the page is open (the button inside refreshes it).
            </div>
